# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
#
# Added 2026-09-23. Everything above this line is the stock GitHub Node
# template, which has NO Python coverage at all — and this repo has run a
# Python service since Phase 5.
#
# Verified before adding: without these rules, `git add .` stages
#   Optimization Engine/__pycache__/engine.cpython-311.pyc
#   forecast-service/__pycache__/forecast.cpython-311.pyc
# Compiled bytecode is machine- and version-specific, so committing it creates
# noisy diffs on every run and can shadow a real source change.
#
# Placed at the ROOT rather than in each service folder deliberately: a
# per-folder file would have protected forecast-service/ while leaving
# "Optimization Engine/" exposed, which is where the problem has actually been
# since Phase 5.
#
# dataset/ has its own .gitignore with its own Python block; these rules are
# harmless there and the two simply agree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Python virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# NOTE — deliberately NOT ignored anywhere in this repo:
#   forecast-service/forecast_model.json   the deployed calibration artefact;
#     Render serves that folder as its root and cannot read dataset/models/,
#     so ignoring it would deploy a service that throws on first request.
#   dataset/models/*.joblib                the record those were exported from.
